{"id": "EUVD-2026-81713", "enisaUuid": "52d57cb7-0244-3beb-ac9b-57eec3cea955", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/gic-v5: Check get_logical_index() return value in MADT IAFFID parsing\n\nIn gic_acpi_parse_iaffid() a given MADT GICC entry might not correspond\nto a logical cpu recognized by the kernel, resulting in the cpu variable\ninitialization to an error value.\n\nCurrently, the get_logical_index() return value is not checked for failure,\nwhich might result in out-of-bounds memory corruption while trying to\nindex a per_cpu variable array.\n\nAdd a check to evaluate get_logical_index() return value.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:18", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6caeb878f809bdf0aec2fdd96f3d41ef4b69fc69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/328affc639ce9873a7a0a3fd6b8339f19767529b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90120", "GHSA-rfj6-7g8r-3866"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "055154af-c9a1-3280-a602-e2be98d1feaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "16673928-9dcc-3135-a6dc-9a1f4431d073", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "5b4a2865-4bb5-35ee-b495-a7e5faba894f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "35866efa52feaf48cc54a0745851a555654e1446 <328affc639ce9873a7a0a3fd6b8339f19767529b"}, {"id": "8ebbad76-6bfb-38f5-8ea3-483648eeb9a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "94d96dde-1193-3169-a838-7bd5fe14add1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "35866efa52feaf48cc54a0745851a555654e1446 <6caeb878f809bdf0aec2fdd96f3d41ef4b69fc69"}, {"id": "d9b9eb93-081a-